      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Macleay Street, the suburb’s eastern boundary, honors Alexander Macleay, the colonial secretary who originally owned the land.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potts_Point",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the early 1820s Governor Macquarie established a farm for Aboriginal people at Elizabeth Bay, later abandoned by 1824.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
